        "uuid": "174f2c2d_a78fb627",
        "filename": "java/java_test.go",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 1832,
      "author": {
        "id": 1878380
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-11-16T01:09:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Since the naming of the final artifact *-android.jar prefixes the api surface, I believe this prop is essential to java_api_library.\n\nCant this be just the name of the soong module?\n```\njava_api_library {\n  name: \"system-stubs\",\n  // api_surface: \"system\",\n  api_providers: [\n    \"my_public_contribution\",\n    \"my_system_contribution\"\n  ],\n}\n```\n\n\u003e I believe it is somewhat self-explanatory from the prefixes of the *{-}current.txt api files\n\nThis enforces a magic naming convention. Which is fine, but imo having an explicit attribute is better than inferring something from filename.",
      "parentUuid": "24394291_6e65a764",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1832,
        "startChar": 2,
